es.","materiality":"Low; both behaviors are directly supported."},{"excerpt":"Hun prooien bieden bovendien voedsel aan andere dieren: van raven en coyotes tot beren en ongewervelden.","claim":"Wolf prey and kills provide food for ravens, coyotes, bears, and invertebrates.","category":"technical","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Many other animals benefit from wolf kills. For example, when wolves kill an elk, ravens and magpies arrive almost immediately. Coyotes arrive soon after, waiting nearby until the wolves are sated. Bears will attempt to chase the wolves away, and are usually successful. Many other animals—from eagles to invertebrates—consume the remains.","narrative":"hun prooien voeden ook andere dieren","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The named groups are all included in the source’s account of animals consuming wolf-kill remains.","materiality":"Low; this is a source-supported food-web relationship."},{"excerpt":"De samenstelling van de prooien veranderde ook.","claim":"The composition of wolves’ prey changed over time.","category":"chronology","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"From 1995 to 2000, in early winter, elk calves comprised 50% of wolf prey, and bull elk comprised 25%. That ratio reversed from 2001 to 2007, indicating changes in prey vulnerability and availability.","narrative":"De veranderde samenstelling van hun prooi in verschillende perioden maakt concreet dat predatiepatronen veranderen","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source reports a reversal in the proportions of elk calves and bull elk in early-winter prey across the two periods.","materiality":"Low; this accurately summarizes the documented change."},{"excerpt":"Onder de prooien die in de vroege winter werden gedood, verschoof tussen 1995–2000 en 2001–2007 de verhouding tussen elandkalveren en volwassen mannelijke elanden.","claim":"Among early-winter prey, the relative proportions of elk calves and adult bull elk shifted between 1995–2000 and 2001–2007.","category":"quantity","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"From 1995 to 2000, in early winter, elk calves comprised 50% of wolf prey, and bull elk comprised 25%. That ratio reversed from 2001 to 2007","narrative":"Gebruik daarnaast de verschuiving in de verhouding tussen elandkalveren en volwassen mannelijke elanden onder de vroege-winterprooien in 1995–2000 en 2001–2007 als concreet voorbeeld van veranderende prooisamenstelling","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source specifies that calves made up 50% and bull elk 25% in the first period, with that ratio reversed in the second. The piece accurately describes a shift without adding unsupported percentages.","materiality":"Moderate; the period and prey categories are specific, but the summary preserves the reported relationship."},{"excerpt":"Die verandering hangt samen met de beschikbaarheid en kwetsbaarheid van prooien.","claim":"The prey-composition change was associated with prey availability and vulnerability.","category":"cause","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"That ratio reversed from 2001 to 2007, indicating changes in prey vulnerability and availability.","narrative":"de bron verbindt die veranderingen met de beschikbaarheid en kwetsbaarheid van prooien.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source says the reversal indicates changes in vulnerability and availability; the piece does not claim either was the sole cause.","materiality":"Low; the association is accurately qualified."},{"excerpt":"De predatiepatronen en de effecten op elanden vallen samen met andere factoren, waaronder andere roofdieren, het beheer van hoefdieren buiten het park en het weer.","claim":"Changes in wolf predation patterns and effects on elk are linked to other predators, ungulate management outside the park, and weather.","category":"cause","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Changes in wolf predation patterns and impacts on prey species like elk are inextricably linked to other factors, such as other predators, management of ungulates outside the park, and weather (e.g. drought, winter severity).","narrative":"veranderingen in predatie en de effecten op elanden samenvallen met andere factoren, waaronder andere roofdieren, beheer van hoefdieren buiten het park en het weer.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source names the same factors. “Vallen samen” is somewhat less explicit about linkage than the source, but does not misstate the relationship.","materiality":"Moderate; this qualification prevents an overly simple account of elk impacts."},{"excerpt":"De wolven maken daarmee deel uit van een samenspel van sociale en voedselrelaties, zonder dat zij alleen de uitkomsten voor elanden bepalen.","claim":"Wolves participate in interacting social and food relationships and do not alone determine outcomes for elk.","category":"interpretation","label":"F0 faithful","evidence":"Consequently, changes in prey selection and kill rates through time result from complex interactions among these factors.","narrative":"Zo blijft het verhaal bij een complex samenspel, niet bij wolven als enige bepalende kracht.","narrativeRelation":"supports","origin":"none","explanation":"The source attributes changing prey selection and kill rates to complex interactions among multiple factors, supporting the piece’s caution against treating wolves as the sole determinant. The social and food relationships are also described in the source.","materiality":"Moderate; this is the piece’s main interpretive conclusion and is consistent with the source’s stated complexity."}]}

